  "question": {
    "text": "The Henry's law constant for the solubility of $\\mathrm{N}_2$ gas in water at $298 \\mathrm{~K}$ is $1.0 \\times 105 \\mathrm{~atm}$. The mole fraction of $\\mathrm{N}_2$ in air is $0.8$. The number of moles of $\\mathrm{N}_2$ from air dissolved in 10 moles of water of $298 \\mathrm{~K}$ and $5 \\mathrm{~atm}$ pressure is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "V0t15",
      "text": "\n$4 \\times 10^{-4}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "QwCiy",
      "text": "\n$4.0 \\times 10^{-5}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AjQOW",
      "text": "\n$5.0 \\times 10^{-4}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "DcLjU",
      "text": "\n$4.0 \\times 10^{-6}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$P_{\\mathrm{N}_2}=K_{\\mathrm{H}} \\times$ mole-fraction $\\left(\\mathrm{N}_2\\right)$ mole-fraction\n$$\n\\mathrm{N}_2 \\frac{1}{10^5} \\times 0.8 \\times 5=4 \\times 10^{-5} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}\n$$\nIn 10 mole solubility in $4 \\times 10^{-4}$.",
    "image": null
